+# Story RC4.1: Detail Payload Extension (Backend Contract)
+
+**Status:** review
+**Epic:** RC4 (Landlord Reference Panel & Workflow). Opens RC4. Depends on RC2.1+ (merged) and the full RC3 chain (rc3-7 merged; #603 was the last).
+**Model:** `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (ledger override of the briefing's glm line — new permanent policy, execution roles).
+**Perkins:** ON (API boundary + privacy stripping — the §4.2 lens-guard).
+**GitHub issue:** #548
+
+## Story
+
+> As the client app,
+> I want `reference_calls[]` in the application detail payload with server-computed hooks and disclaimers,
+> So that the panel renders from one stable contract and never re-derives state rules.
+
+rc1-1…rc3-7 shipped the collection engine: the attestation + capture columns (rc1-1), the `reference_call` system of record (rc2-1), the viewed trigger (rc2-2/2.3), the referee form session + exit routes (rc3-3/3.4), the sweep (rc3-5), the verified webhooks (rc3-6), and the honest fraud-signals module (rc3-7). RC4.1 **opens RC4** by building the landlord-facing detail payload contract — the bridge from the collection engine to the panel UI (RC4.2–4.4): it surfaces templates/sweep/webhook/fraud-signal data, **strips internal-only fields at the boundary**, and computes the hooks + disclaimers the panel needs. One stable server-computed contract; the panel never re-derives state rules client-side (AR-RC13).
+
+**The load-bearing rule (§4.2 boundary strip):** `form_token`, `objection_detail.payload_ref`, and raw IPs/UAs inside `fraud_signals.form_session` NEVER reach the client. The derived booleans (`ip_matches_applicant`, `device_fingerprint_match`) transit; the raw comparators do not. A spoofed/malformed payload can't leak internals. Server tests carry **explicit stripping assertions**.
+
+## Scope
+
+### OWNS
+1. **`shared/src/shared/reference_call.gleam`** — extend with the §8.1 payload entry type: `ReferenceCallDetail` (or equivalent) + JSON codecs: `reference_call_id`, `ref_slot`, `owner_label`, `status`, `outcome`, `attempt_count`, `next_attempt_at`, the attempt log (`attempts`), the stored `result` (stripped), `display_disclaimer`, and the `hooks` object. AR21: snake_case unbroken DB → JSON → Gleam, zero translation at any boundary.
+2. **`shared/src/shared/application_detail.gleam`** — extend `ApplicationDetail` with `reference_calls: List(ReferenceCallDetail)` + `attestation_on_file: Bool` (per-application, AD-2) so the panel renders the Off + pre-trigger states without extra fetches. `reference_contact_choice` + the referee trios already ride on `shared/application.gleam` (rc1-2) — nothing to add there.
+3. **`server/src/application/application_detail_handler.gleam`** — `handle_get_detail` gains:
+   - `reference_calls[]` per §8.1 (from `list_reference_calls_for_application.sql` or a dedicated read),
+   - the **§4.2 boundary strip** (form_token / objection_detail.payload_ref / raw IPs+UAs stripped — never serialized),
+   - `display_disclaimer` server-rendered per channel (§9.5: written-channel results carry the call-encouragement note — the §8.1 calibration copy verbatim; provenance framing, never invalidation),
+   - hooks computed per §8.2 — `can_record_manual` (any non-terminal), `can_substitute_referee` (terminal `objected`/`unreachable`), `can_retry` (`failed`),
+   - `attestation_on_file` per application (EXISTS `acknowledgement_record` with `record_type='reference_contact_attestation'`; `revoked_at` is never written in v1).
+4. **SQL** — a reference-call read for the detail payload + an `attestation_on_file` read (or fold into `get_application_detail.sql`). Keep the existing `list_reference_calls_for_application.sql` for the trigger/form handlers (it carries `form_token` internally).
+5. **Round-trip tests** (AR21) — shared codec tests in `shared/test/reference_call_test.gleam` + `shared/test/application_detail_test.gleam`.
+6. **Server tests with explicit stripping assertions** (§4.2 lens-guard) — the serialized payload never contains `form_token`, `objection_detail.payload_ref`, `referee_ip`, `referee_user_agent`.
+7. **Hook-logic edge-state tests** — `can_record_manual` / `can_substitute_referee` / `can_retry` across every lifecycle state incl. terminal `objected`/`unreachable`/`failed` + non-terminal `queued`/`skipped`/`contact_initiated`/`awaiting_correction` + `partial`.
+8. **rc3-7 advisory sweep (trivial, same area):**
+   - **module doc** — `webhooks.gleam:12-13` module doc still names the deleted `claim_webhook_event` as the idempotency mechanism (r2 #1): rewrite to name the find/mark live-status scoping (`WHERE status IN ('queued','contact_initiated')`).
+   - **orphaned table comment** — `webhooks.gleam:38` + `webhooks_test.gleam:66` still document `processed_reference_webhook_event` as the live idempotency table (r2 #2). The table's only writer (`claim_webhook_event`) was removed in rc3-7; **the DROP TABLE itself is a destructive two-deploy — NOT this PR** (rc3-6 is merged). Clear the stale comments; the table is already write-dead.
+   - **test-helper idiom** — `reference_exit_routes_integration_test.gleam` `form_session_text` string-interpolates the token into SQL (r2 #4): bind with `pog.parameter`.
+   - **metadata** — `sprint-status-refcheck-v1.yaml` `last_updated` regressed 2026-08-12 → 2026-08-11 (r2 #5): set to the actual edit date.
+
+### Does NOT own (deferred / sibling stories)
+- **The panel UI** (render, testids, expand/collapse, copy) → RC4.2.
+- **Row actions** (start now, skip, take over, correct, substitute) → RC4.3.
+- **Attempt-log export + notification completeness** → RC4.4.
+- **The NULLIF-convention note** (r2 #3 — `get_application_reference_contacts.sql`/`count_cross_application_contact_reuse.sql` use plain COALESCE) → RC4.3 owns it (the correction write lands there).
+- **DROP TABLE `processed_reference_webhook_event`** → destructive two-deploy, separate PR (rc3-6 is merged; the writer is gone).
+- **v2 voice channel** → `display_disclaimer` for `voice` is v2-reserved; v1 emits written-channel copy only.
