+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epic RC4.1 + arch §8.1/§8.2/§9.5/§4.2/A4/A5/AR21, FR-RC13)
+
+**AC1 — `reference_calls[]` per §8.1**
+> **Given** `GET /api/v1/vacancies/:vid/applications/:aid`
+> **When** the application has reference data
+> **Then** the payload gains `reference_calls[]` per architecture §8.1: `reference_call_id`, `ref_slot`, `owner_label`, `status`, `outcome`, `attempt_count`, `next_attempt_at`, the attempt log, the stored `result`, and the hooks object
+> **And** internal-only fields are stripped at the boundary — `form_token`, `objection_detail.payload_ref`, raw IPs/UAs inside `fraud_signals.form_session` (§4.2)
+
+**AC2 — `display_disclaimer` + hooks per channel/state**
+> **Given** each entry
+> **When** it serialises
+> **Then** `display_disclaimer` is server-rendered per channel (§9.5): written-channel results carry the call-encouragement note (calibration copy per §8.1 — verbatim, em-dash included; provenance framing, never invalidation), and the hooks are computed per §8.2 — `can_record_manual` any non-terminal, `can_substitute_referee` terminal `objected`/`unreachable`, `can_retry` `failed`
+
+**AC3 — application-level fields**
+> **Given** the application itself
+> **When** the payload builds
+> **Then** it carries `attestation_on_file` and `reference_contact_choice` (A4) plus the referee trios, so the panel can render the Off state and the pre-trigger state without extra fetches
+
+**AC4 — compilation boundary (AR21)**
+> **Given** the compilation boundary
+> **When** types are defined
+> **Then** they live in the shared package with JSON codecs (snake_case unbroken DB → JSON → Gleam, canonical AR21) and round-trip tests
+
+## Hook logic reference (§8.2 — the exact rule)
+
+| Status | Terminal? | `can_record_manual` | `can_substitute_referee` | `can_retry` |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `queued` | no | ✅ | — | — |
+| `skipped` | no (A6, re-enables) | ✅ | — | — |
+| `contact_initiated` | no | ✅ | — | — |
+| `awaiting_correction` | no | ✅ | — | — |
+| `scheduled` (v2) | no | ✅ | — | — |
+| `calling` (v2) | no | ✅ | — | — |
+| `form_completed` | yes | — | — | — |
+| `partial` | yes | — | — | — |
+| `unreachable` | yes | — | ✅ | — |
+| `refused` | yes | — | — | — |
+| `objected` | yes | — | ✅ | — |
+| `manual_recorded` | yes | — | — | — |
+| `failed` | yes | — | — | ✅ |
+| `completed` (v2) | yes | — | — | — |
+
+Terminal set (for `can_record_manual`): `form_completed`, `partial`, `unreachable`, `refused`, `objected`, `manual_recorded`, `failed`, `completed` (v2-reserved). Everything else is non-terminal. `skipped` is NOT terminal (A6 — re-enables to `queued`).
